1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,508
Chapterestablishers

2
00:01:33,508 --> 00:01:35,508
Grudged Kocher

3
00:01:35,508 --> 00:01:39,508
Treasure MUS shooter

4
00:01:39,508 --> 00:01:41,508
üpunderted

5
00:01:41,508 --> 00:01:47,508
Explozu

6
00:01:47,508 --> 00:01:49,508
...

7
00:01:49,508 --> 00:01:51,508
...

8
00:01:51,508 --> 00:01:53,508
...

9
00:01:53,508 --> 00:01:55,508
...

10
00:01:55,508 --> 00:01:57,508
...

11
00:01:57,508 --> 00:01:59,508
...

12
00:01:59,508 --> 00:02:27,608
The sunset was even more beautiful than I remembered.

13
00:02:29,508 --> 00:02:41,508
Next thing I knew, I was standing with a hoe in my hand.

14
00:02:41,508 --> 00:02:46,508
That's when I realized I was dreaming.

15
00:02:46,508 --> 00:02:55,508
It was a feeling I knew well, so I got right to work.

16
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:59,508
Someone's calling me.

17
00:02:59,508 --> 00:03:02,508
Oh, it's my girlfriend.

18
00:03:02,508 --> 00:03:06,508
We broke up five years ago.

19
00:03:06,508 --> 00:03:08,508
Now I see.

20
00:03:08,508 --> 00:03:15,508
In this dream, we never broke up.

21
00:03:15,508 --> 00:03:27,508
Oh, so in this world, I never made it as a pro and decided to return home.

22
00:03:27,508 --> 00:03:31,508
All the lights are on.

23
00:03:31,508 --> 00:03:34,508
I feel like I could cry.

24
00:03:34,508 --> 00:03:39,508
Everyone's here and doing well.

25
00:03:39,508 --> 00:03:45,508
My grandma and grandpa, I miss them so much.

26
00:03:45,508 --> 00:03:48,508
Wow, Kai's incredibly good.

27
00:03:48,508 --> 00:03:51,508
No one here even stands a chance against him.

28
00:03:51,508 --> 00:03:53,508
He's great, isn't he?

29
00:03:53,508 --> 00:03:59,508
Father, grandpa, everyone, I have to apologize.

30
00:03:59,508 --> 00:04:05,508
You've been cheering me on and have had so much faith in me.

31
00:04:05,508 --> 00:04:06,508
It's alright.

32
00:04:06,508 --> 00:04:12,508
Really, you may not have made it as a pro, but you can still be happy.

33
00:04:12,508 --> 00:04:16,508
No matter what path you choose, you can find contentment.

34
00:04:16,508 --> 00:04:23,508
As long as you live each day to the fullest without looking back, we'll always be proud of you.

35
00:04:23,508 --> 00:04:44,508
You'll be fine, Kai.

36
00:04:44,508 --> 00:04:51,508
The funny thing is, even in my dreams, I can't stop playing Shogi.

37
00:04:51,508 --> 00:04:57,508
I also regretted not going pro.

38
00:04:57,508 --> 00:05:03,508
It's no surprise that the whole ordeal made my stomach hurt.

39
00:05:03,508 --> 00:05:05,508
I feel bad for Shimada 8th Dan.

40
00:05:05,508 --> 00:05:07,508
This whole thing must be like a nightmare.

41
00:05:07,508 --> 00:05:09,508
Yeah, he's dead in the water.

42
00:05:09,508 --> 00:05:14,508
And with four straight losses, he won't get to have a match in his hometown.

43
00:05:14,508 --> 00:05:19,508
If you can't say anything nice, don't say anything at all.

44
00:05:19,508 --> 00:05:25,508
If only that were the case, but I won't expect an apology anytime soon.

45
00:05:25,508 --> 00:05:31,508
Oh, my damn stomach.

46
00:05:31,508 --> 00:05:35,508
Alright then, I guess it's time to get ready.

47
00:05:35,508 --> 00:05:43,508
The Mii who couldn't become a pro and moved back to the countryside.

48
00:05:43,508 --> 00:05:49,508
The Mii who risked it all to make it this far, only to face four straight losses.

49
00:05:49,508 --> 00:05:53,508
Which is the true nightmare?

50
00:05:53,508 --> 00:05:55,508
Let's find out by seeing it through to the end.

51
00:05:55,508 --> 00:06:05,508
The Shishio Tournament. Match 4, Day 2.

52
00:06:05,508 --> 00:06:11,508
Yesterday, Meijin Soya secured his defense and then launched the first attack.

53
00:06:11,508 --> 00:06:17,508
But Mr. Shimada countered. He's in the lead, but not by much.

54
00:06:17,508 --> 00:06:23,508
Knight to 7-3. Just as Mr. Shimada started to attack, the game was adjourned.

55
00:06:23,508 --> 00:06:31,508
Don't you think Mr. Shimada is using his Knight to 7-3 a little too soon?

56
00:06:31,508 --> 00:06:37,508
Yeah, I think you're right. It just feels like he's panicking instead of really thinking about his attacks.

57
00:06:37,508 --> 00:06:39,508
Would you like some miso soup?

58
00:06:39,508 --> 00:06:41,508
No, sorry. Yeah, sure.

59
00:06:41,508 --> 00:06:46,508
It's like he doesn't want to draw it out. And he does look kinda sick, even if that's the case.

60
00:06:47,508 --> 00:06:50,508
Shimada's doing the best he can, but I doubt he'll win.

61
00:06:50,508 --> 00:06:52,508
Well, not against Soya anyway.

62
00:06:52,508 --> 00:06:55,508
We're probably looking at four straight losses.

63
00:06:56,508 --> 00:07:01,508
He's gonna miss another chance at a showdown in his hometown. Yamagata's a long way off.

64
00:07:02,508 --> 00:07:05,508
Almost everyone seems to be thinking the same thing.

65
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:08,508
They're all ready to declare Soya the winner.

66
00:07:09,508 --> 00:07:12,508
And sure, Mr. Shimada has been aggressive this match.

67
00:07:14,508 --> 00:07:17,508
But I wouldn't say he's panicking. He's playing like normal.

68
00:07:18,508 --> 00:07:20,508
At least that's how it looks to me.

69
00:07:21,508 --> 00:07:23,508
The battle of nerves continues.

70
00:07:24,508 --> 00:07:29,508
Mr. Shimada, fearless in the face of Meijin Soya, was able to earn a few points.

71
00:07:29,508 --> 00:07:34,508
It's not as bad as they think.

72
00:07:34,508 --> 00:07:35,508
Huh?

73
00:07:35,508 --> 00:07:36,508
Kiriyama?

74
00:07:37,508 --> 00:07:38,508
Why didn't you tell me, Mr. Shimada?

75
00:07:38,508 --> 00:07:39,508
Kibata wasn't feeling well!

76
00:07:40,508 --> 00:07:43,508
I would have taken him to Kyoto in a limo with a bed!

77
00:07:43,508 --> 00:07:44,888
Shimada wasn't feeling well.

78
00:07:47,328 --> 00:07:50,148
I would have taken him to Kyoto in a limo with a bed.

79
00:07:50,328 --> 00:07:51,248
I know what you're doing.

80
00:07:51,468 --> 00:07:53,628
You've been practicing together behind my back.

81
00:07:53,768 --> 00:07:55,048
So why'd you leave me out?

82
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:59,668
Don't forget that he's my coach and I've been a part of his workshop way longer than you have.

83
00:07:59,808 --> 00:08:00,348
You got it?

84
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:01,908
Sorry about that, Nikaido.

85
00:08:02,248 --> 00:08:04,588
I was going to call you sooner, but I haven't had the chance.

86
00:08:04,588 --> 00:08:07,588
And, uh, Mr. Shimada is... well...

87
00:08:08,368 --> 00:08:09,288
Please, don't.

88
00:08:09,628 --> 00:08:11,048
He'll just make a big fuss.

89
00:08:11,048 --> 00:08:14,468
The stress from that alone would make a hole in my stomach.

90
00:08:14,848 --> 00:08:17,288
So please, don't tell Nikaido.

91
00:08:17,908 --> 00:08:21,708
Mr. Shimada, are you okay? I'll be there as soon as I can!

92
00:08:21,968 --> 00:08:27,828
One time, he was so worried that he landed his helicopter in the courtyard of the neighborhood elementary school.

93
00:08:31,608 --> 00:08:34,528
I would have flown to him this time if I didn't have a match.

94
00:08:36,748 --> 00:08:38,768
Kiriyama, take care of him.

95
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:42,048
Stay with him, even after the match is over.

96
00:08:43,188 --> 00:08:48,948
Knowing him, no matter what happens, I know he'll play to the very end.

97
00:08:51,648 --> 00:08:52,928
Yeah, got it.

98
00:08:54,608 --> 00:08:56,128
I'll make sure to keep an eye on him.

99
00:08:56,628 --> 00:08:57,408
I'll bring him home.

100
00:08:57,408 --> 00:09:04,048
Chairman, please, let me do the morning broadcast.

101
00:09:04,368 --> 00:09:06,288
At least let me re-assure the match.

102
00:09:07,108 --> 00:09:08,888
I'm fine. I can do this.

103
00:09:09,328 --> 00:09:10,688
I can do it!

104
00:09:11,148 --> 00:09:13,788
I wore a new kimono just for the occasion.

105
00:09:14,608 --> 00:09:16,088
Let me be on TV!

106
00:09:18,488 --> 00:09:19,408
Tsuji Ninth Den.

107
00:09:19,668 --> 00:09:20,788
He's the official observer.

108
00:09:21,028 --> 00:09:21,768
He has the flu.

109
00:09:22,168 --> 00:09:23,988
They just found out and he wouldn't leave.

110
00:09:27,048 --> 00:09:29,248
Everybody, gargle and wash your hands!

111
00:09:29,648 --> 00:09:31,088
Does anyone else have the flu?

112
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:32,348
I need to know!

113
00:09:32,768 --> 00:09:35,268
If any of you infect the players, I'll kill you myself!

114
00:09:35,268 --> 00:09:39,128
That guy!

115
00:09:39,328 --> 00:09:43,208
He's been clearing his throat since yesterday morning, but I thought maybe he was just being

116
00:09:43,208 --> 00:09:43,788
snobby.

117
00:09:44,008 --> 00:09:48,288
I can't believe he'd want to be on TV so badly that he'd cover up having the flu.

118
00:09:48,748 --> 00:09:49,228
I know.

119
00:09:49,328 --> 00:09:50,048
It's too bad.

120
00:09:50,108 --> 00:09:51,448
He's handsome enough for TV.

121
00:09:51,728 --> 00:09:53,288
Talk about a waste of good looks.

122
00:09:53,288 --> 00:09:59,148
I'm promoting you, Smith.

123
00:09:59,568 --> 00:10:02,028
Your time as an assistant observer is over.

124
00:10:02,268 --> 00:10:03,908
You're now the official observer.

125
00:10:04,448 --> 00:10:04,968
What?

126
00:10:05,308 --> 00:10:06,048
So suddenly?

127
00:10:06,408 --> 00:10:07,848
It starts in ten minutes.

128
00:10:08,088 --> 00:10:08,588
All right.

129
00:10:08,668 --> 00:10:09,648
Head to the match room.

130
00:10:10,068 --> 00:10:10,428
Wait.

131
00:10:10,748 --> 00:10:12,448
I have to open the sealed move envelope?

132
00:10:12,728 --> 00:10:14,528
That's way too important on my first day.

133
00:10:14,828 --> 00:10:15,848
Let's get started.

134
00:10:15,968 --> 00:10:19,868
Not to mention, I'm an observer for someone else's title match before I have my own.

135
00:10:20,468 --> 00:10:21,468
This is terrible.

136
00:10:21,468 --> 00:10:23,068
It's a bad omen.

137
00:10:23,528 --> 00:10:24,568
It's going to be fine.

138
00:10:24,628 --> 00:10:25,168
Don't worry.

139
00:10:25,568 --> 00:10:28,148
Hardly any of the professional players here have had a title match.

140
00:10:28,208 --> 00:10:29,028
It's very rare.

141
00:10:29,348 --> 00:10:30,328
Except for me.

142
00:10:30,428 --> 00:10:31,388
I've had a few.

143
00:10:34,048 --> 00:10:38,748
I'm opening the envelope of another player's sealed move before I get to use one.

144
00:10:39,508 --> 00:10:43,348
It's kind of like signing off as a witness on a friend's marriage license before getting

145
00:10:43,348 --> 00:10:44,308
married myself.

146
00:10:44,688 --> 00:10:45,068
You know?

147
00:10:45,748 --> 00:10:48,468
But even still, it is a great honor.

148
00:10:51,468 --> 00:11:03,588
And now, here's the envelope.

149
00:11:03,588 --> 00:11:09,928
The sealed move.

150
00:11:10,348 --> 00:11:11,268
Silver to 6-6.

151
00:11:15,268 --> 00:11:19,988
And then, the curtain calmly rose on the second day.

152
00:11:23,108 --> 00:11:23,868
Wait a minute.

153
00:11:23,988 --> 00:11:24,828
What about...

154
00:11:24,828 --> 00:11:25,328
Oh, hey!

155
00:11:26,508 --> 00:11:27,028
Kiriyama!

156
00:11:27,028 --> 00:11:35,328
And so, I would like to begin with an explanation of the demonstration board for this second day

157
00:11:35,328 --> 00:11:38,268
of the fourth match of the 20th Shishio Tournament.

158
00:11:38,268 --> 00:11:44,668
First of all, the demonstration board commentator will be...

159
00:11:44,668 --> 00:11:46,548
Kiryu Champion, Raido Fujimoto!

160
00:11:51,428 --> 00:11:56,028
Since the observer of this match, Suji Ninth Den has the flu, we had to act fast and ask

161
00:11:56,028 --> 00:11:59,868
Rei Kiriyama Fifth Den to replace him as co-commentator on the demonstration board.

162
00:12:00,068 --> 00:12:01,428
We hope you enjoy the proceedings.

163
00:12:01,748 --> 00:12:02,868
Anything you'd like to add?

164
00:12:04,208 --> 00:12:05,228
Nice to meet you all.

165
00:12:05,268 --> 00:12:05,948
I'll do my best.

166
00:12:05,948 --> 00:12:14,208
As you may know, Kiriyama Fifth Den is known for becoming only the fifth professional shogi

167
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:16,188
player to get his start in middle school.

168
00:12:17,168 --> 00:12:21,448
The other four that were middle school pros, including Meijin Soya, all went on to become

169
00:12:21,448 --> 00:12:22,688
grandmasters themselves.

170
00:12:22,988 --> 00:12:25,548
Some even say middle school pros are future grandmasters.

171
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,608
Do you think you'll be following in their footsteps?

172
00:12:29,068 --> 00:12:32,528
Well, for me, my older colleagues were much more skilled.

173
00:12:32,948 --> 00:12:34,808
I'm actually pretty small in comparison.

174
00:12:35,148 --> 00:12:35,448
Sorry.

175
00:12:35,948 --> 00:12:36,948
Ah, come on.

176
00:12:37,288 --> 00:12:41,388
It doesn't matter if he was a middle school student when he made his debut, not when he

177
00:12:41,388 --> 00:12:44,048
suddenly got stuck after reaching C1.

178
00:12:44,048 --> 00:12:49,488
Well, as a first year high school student, I made my debut, but I was at B2.

179
00:12:49,488 --> 00:12:51,928
So what I'm really trying to say is...

180
00:12:51,928 --> 00:12:56,088
I'm more impressive!

181
00:12:56,928 --> 00:12:58,828
That's my point!

182
00:12:58,828 --> 00:13:04,268
And while we're at it, why is the world so enamored with the expression middle school

183
00:13:04,268 --> 00:13:05,268
debut?

184
00:13:05,268 --> 00:13:06,708
It's baffling to me!

185
00:13:06,708 --> 00:13:09,148
Future grandmaster?

186
00:13:09,148 --> 00:13:10,148
A grandmaster?

187
00:13:10,148 --> 00:13:11,588
Nobody knows that for sure!

188
00:13:11,588 --> 00:13:12,588
For sure!

189
00:13:12,588 --> 00:13:15,028
The goal of becoming a pro is all well and good.

190
00:13:15,028 --> 00:13:20,468
But if your goal isn't becoming a grandmaster at all costs, why are you even playing Shogi?

191
00:13:20,468 --> 00:13:25,908
It can be assumed that having no desire is a rather beautiful thing, but it doesn't make any sense

192
00:13:25,908 --> 00:13:29,248
that a goal is good and yet a desire is bad.

193
00:13:29,248 --> 00:13:31,348
Aren't they the same exact thing?

194
00:13:31,348 --> 00:13:32,348
Yeah!

195
00:13:32,348 --> 00:13:33,348
That desire is obvious.

196
00:13:33,348 --> 00:13:38,188
Our mystical matey has hindered my every move, but I swear I'll drag him off that throne

197
00:13:38,188 --> 00:13:39,588
and become grandmaster myself!

198
00:13:39,588 --> 00:13:40,588
Yeah, yeah!

199
00:13:40,588 --> 00:13:43,588
Until that happens, you can bet that I won't drop from A rank!

200
00:13:43,588 --> 00:13:47,228
In fact, once I'm matey, I'll hold on to the title till I die!

201
00:13:51,228 --> 00:13:52,228
Ha ha!

202
00:13:52,228 --> 00:13:53,228
That's all!

203
00:13:53,228 --> 00:14:09,668
Wow, Mr. Shimada, you were surrounded by people like this and fought them on a daily basis?

204
00:14:09,668 --> 00:14:14,188
The fact that you only suffer from stomach aches makes you just as monstrous as they are!

205
00:14:14,188 --> 00:14:15,748
I can't do it!

206
00:14:15,748 --> 00:14:18,388
Class A is too crazy!

207
00:14:18,388 --> 00:14:20,388
AAAAAAAAAAAAAH!!!

208
00:14:38,388 --> 00:14:39,348
It hurts...

209
00:14:41,508 --> 00:14:43,368
...it hurts

210
00:14:43,888 --> 00:14:45,548
It hurts...

211
00:14:46,748 --> 00:14:47,548
It hurts...

212
00:14:48,388 --> 00:15:05,748
Son of a bitch. I swear. Damn it. It's like a dark swamp. Dropping. Churning. In the pit of my stomach.

213
00:15:10,088 --> 00:15:12,988
All this pain just makes me feel alive.

214
00:15:12,988 --> 00:15:21,268
Oh. He's going with pawn to 5-7 promoted? That's crazy. If he lets up on the attack, he'll be surrounded.

215
00:15:21,708 --> 00:15:25,328
His king's on pretty shaky ground. How long can he keep up the attack?

216
00:15:27,308 --> 00:15:34,088
Silver to 6-7. Threatmate. Silver to 7-8. Rook to 2-8. Threatmate again.

217
00:15:34,988 --> 00:15:39,448
Can Shimada finish him off like this? Still, his opponent is Soya.

218
00:15:39,788 --> 00:15:42,588
Yeah, but can he win? Not a chance.

219
00:15:42,988 --> 00:15:44,428
Rook to 7-1.

220
00:15:47,688 --> 00:15:51,148
He wrote it out. Using just a rook and a pawn.

221
00:15:52,048 --> 00:15:53,988
And now, it's Soya's turn.

222
00:15:55,728 --> 00:16:01,008
That was it. Where Shimada Eifdan's attack stopped.

223
00:16:02,588 --> 00:16:06,208
And Meijin Soya's counterattack began.

224
00:16:10,268 --> 00:16:11,528
That's the game.

225
00:16:12,988 --> 00:16:14,248
I'm out of here.

226
00:16:14,248 --> 00:16:14,308
I'm out of here.

227
00:16:20,048 --> 00:16:21,048
Snow.

228
00:16:24,048 --> 00:16:26,148
No matter how I struggle,

229
00:16:27,028 --> 00:16:29,608
it'll bury me mercilessly.

230
00:16:30,808 --> 00:16:32,888
It's a blinding darkness.

231
00:16:33,828 --> 00:16:35,868
It's almost too much.

232
00:16:35,868 --> 00:16:39,028
So silent.

233
00:16:39,028 --> 00:16:41,248
It's overwhelming.

234
00:16:45,248 --> 00:17:01,628
It's captivatingly beautiful.

235
00:17:01,628 --> 00:17:03,468
Oh, such beauty.

236
00:17:07,468 --> 00:17:08,188
Wait.

237
00:17:08,688 --> 00:17:10,108
Please, wait.

238
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:12,248
Don't go.

239
00:17:13,248 --> 00:17:14,208
It's not over yet.

240
00:17:14,648 --> 00:17:15,068
Huh?

241
00:17:15,628 --> 00:17:17,668
His fortress was torn down.

242
00:17:17,888 --> 00:17:19,188
His king's in danger.

243
00:17:19,508 --> 00:17:20,828
And his opponent, Soya.

244
00:17:20,828 --> 00:17:23,788
There's no way he can turn it around from here.

245
00:17:24,048 --> 00:17:25,748
But still, it's not over yet.

246
00:17:26,508 --> 00:17:28,908
His pieces are still in play, so it's not over.

247
00:17:29,068 --> 00:17:29,788
It is over.

248
00:17:29,948 --> 00:17:31,088
Shimada's done, kid.

249
00:17:31,608 --> 00:17:34,108
It's not like he stood a chance in the first place.

250
00:17:34,668 --> 00:17:35,608
Four straight losses.

251
00:17:35,928 --> 00:17:37,188
He's a stubborn weakling.

252
00:17:37,908 --> 00:17:38,348
What?

253
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:44,208
Aren't you in that shogi workshop Shimada put together?

254
00:17:45,128 --> 00:17:48,328
I understand not wanting to admit your mentor's in trouble,

255
00:17:48,808 --> 00:17:50,508
but you're affecting his reputation.

256
00:17:51,788 --> 00:17:53,388
So keep your mouth shut.

257
00:18:00,268 --> 00:18:03,008
Well, Shimada then did his best.

258
00:18:03,308 --> 00:18:03,768
Yeah.

259
00:18:04,328 --> 00:18:06,608
Fine, if you consider who his opponent was.

260
00:18:06,608 --> 00:18:08,128
He can't be helped.

261
00:18:08,608 --> 00:18:09,708
He was outclassed.

262
00:18:09,908 --> 00:18:11,608
Well, it was Soya, after all.

263
00:18:11,828 --> 00:18:13,008
Four straight losses.

264
00:18:13,648 --> 00:18:16,988
Yeah, but even still, he could have won once.

265
00:18:17,348 --> 00:18:18,948
I wanted to see some backbone.

266
00:18:19,728 --> 00:18:21,348
He didn't show us anything.

267
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:22,808
I'm not surprised.

268
00:18:23,548 --> 00:18:25,228
Yamagato was a long way off.

269
00:18:25,468 --> 00:18:26,928
Well, what did you expect?

270
00:18:28,228 --> 00:18:28,788
No.

271
00:18:30,828 --> 00:18:32,328
No, that's wrong.

272
00:18:32,328 --> 00:18:36,748
This board doesn't look dead.

273
00:18:37,208 --> 00:18:38,188
Not to me, anyway.

274
00:18:39,948 --> 00:18:41,328
I don't think that...

275
00:18:42,528 --> 00:18:44,708
Mr. Shimada's pieces...

276
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:45,348
are dead.

277
00:18:46,988 --> 00:18:48,108
They're alive.

278
00:18:49,548 --> 00:18:50,568
To me.

279
00:18:51,388 --> 00:18:52,328
To me.

280
00:18:53,328 --> 00:18:54,228
To me.

281
00:18:54,228 --> 00:18:54,308
To me.

282
00:18:54,308 --> 00:19:01,988
Uh, Kiriyama?

283
00:19:02,528 --> 00:19:03,188
Wait!

284
00:19:03,588 --> 00:19:04,448
Where are you going?

285
00:19:04,728 --> 00:19:05,988
Kiriyama 5th then!

286
00:19:08,688 --> 00:19:10,308
Mr. Shimada...

287
00:19:10,308 --> 00:19:12,308
Mr. Shimada...

288
00:19:13,608 --> 00:19:14,128
Wait!

289
00:19:15,088 --> 00:19:16,368
Don't give up!

290
00:19:16,368 --> 00:19:20,888
Mr. Fujimoto!

291
00:19:20,888 --> 00:19:21,388
No!

292
00:19:33,528 --> 00:19:35,448
Mr. Shimada...

293
00:19:39,048 --> 00:19:40,908
Shimada, Ethan, conceded.

294
00:19:42,388 --> 00:19:44,408
Like I said, he never stood a chance.

295
00:19:45,848 --> 00:19:47,288
I tried to warn you.

296
00:19:50,888 --> 00:20:06,088
So it went unnoticed, huh?

297
00:20:08,088 --> 00:20:12,928
This darkness isn't just playing on an endless loop.

298
00:20:13,748 --> 00:20:15,308
Hey, wait!

299
00:20:15,708 --> 00:20:16,988
This is...

300
00:20:16,988 --> 00:20:18,308
Seven-Nine-Bishop.

301
00:20:18,308 --> 00:20:20,548
It's a reversal?

302
00:20:21,028 --> 00:20:23,248
The two-four-night's threatmate is gone, too.

303
00:20:23,728 --> 00:20:24,068
Huh?

304
00:20:24,908 --> 00:20:27,408
Isn't Mei-jin-soya's king under check?

305
00:20:30,888 --> 00:20:32,308
And then...

306
00:20:32,308 --> 00:20:34,308
With just one move...

307
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:37,308
The world...

308
00:20:37,988 --> 00:20:40,208
Reveals a completely different form.

309
00:20:41,308 --> 00:20:43,448
A small opening at the end.

310
00:20:44,108 --> 00:20:45,348
A tiny gap.

311
00:20:45,348 --> 00:20:49,848
A spark of light shining through.

312
00:20:52,848 --> 00:20:53,648
Oh, well.

313
00:20:54,148 --> 00:20:55,928
You had too much faith in me.

314
00:21:06,468 --> 00:21:08,288
And it was beautiful, too.

315
00:21:08,288 --> 00:21:26,848
And so, the Shishio Tournament ended with Mr. Shimada's four consecutive losses.

316
00:21:26,848 --> 00:21:34,088
That night, Mr. Shimada and I left Kyoto for the journey home.

317
00:21:34,088 --> 00:21:41,288
I have some water and a light meal.

318
00:21:41,288 --> 00:21:41,328
I have some water and a light meal.

319
00:21:49,328 --> 00:21:56,588
As I watched him lying there, pale and exhausted, I thought about the path he had taken.

320
00:21:56,588 --> 00:22:04,088
That's right.

321
00:22:04,088 --> 00:22:05,988
I knew it from the start.

322
00:22:06,548 --> 00:22:07,408
The truth.

323
00:22:08,988 --> 00:22:11,408
What lies beyond the other side of the storm.

324
00:22:12,088 --> 00:22:12,588
It's just...

325
00:22:14,588 --> 00:22:15,588
Another...

326
00:22:15,588 --> 00:22:18,688
Even more furious storm.

327
00:22:20,088 --> 00:22:25,628
No matter how many times you fall, you have to pick up the pieces and move on.

328
00:22:26,348 --> 00:22:29,948
In this world, you must find a way to keep moving forward.

329
00:22:31,128 --> 00:22:33,388
Wandering without end.

330
00:22:36,088 --> 00:22:37,088
Then why?

331
00:22:37,088 --> 00:22:43,588
The answer to that, isn't something someone else can give you.

332
00:22:46,988 --> 00:22:53,388
The only way to know that, is by asking yourself, in the middle of that raging storm.

333
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:37,091
No matter where I go, the rain always follows me around.

334
00:24:37,231 --> 00:24:40,671
Just go and have a good time. Relax, the fresh air will do you good.

335
00:24:40,891 --> 00:24:45,231
Well, things have settled down here, but I guess Sis likes it like this.

336
00:24:46,211 --> 00:24:47,891
It looks like I've lost.

337
00:24:48,711 --> 00:24:50,151
Thank you very much, everyone.

338
00:24:51,631 --> 00:24:54,091
I can't believe I had to reveal the sealed move.

339
00:24:54,331 --> 00:24:56,331
Don't miss the next march comes in like a lion.

340
00:24:56,891 --> 00:24:58,811
Strawberry, I'm coming home!

341
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
I'm coming home!

